== Final ==
F1: place values of six switches from the right: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32
F2: 10110 = 22; 110011 = 51; 19 = 10011
F3: 7 switches: 128 patterns, biggest 127
F4: 77 ladder: 77/2=38 r1; 38/2=19 r0; 19/2=9 r1; 9/2=4 r1; 4/2=2 r0; 2/2=1 r0; 1/2=0 r1; 77 = 1001101; doubling 1011010: 1 2 5 11 22 45 90 -> 90
F5: 12 = 1100, reversed 0011 = 3; 9 = 1001, reversed 1001 (same)
F6: 1110 = 14 = hex E
F7: 10111001 = 0xB9 = 185; 0x7C = 01111100 = 124; 203 / 16 = 12 r 11 -> 0xCB
F8: red 255 green 8 blue 0 -> #FF0800 (8 printed with one digit: 8)
F9: 1 kB = 1000 B, 1 KiB = 1024 B, 3 MiB = 3145728 B
F10: 2097152 B = 2 MiB = 2.097152 MB = 16777216 bits
F11: 250 kB = 250000 B = 244.140625 KiB
F12: 11111111 unsigned 255, signed -1
F13: 20 = 00010100, flipped 11101011, plus one 11101100 = 0xEC reads -20; 10010110 unsigned 150 signed -106; 100 + 100 = 200 in a signed byte reads -56
F14: 10010100 signed = -108 (unsigned 148)
F15: x = 01101001 = 0x69 = 105; set bit 4: 01111001; clear bit 0: 01101000; toggle bit 7: 11101001; x >> 2 = 00011010, (x >> 2) & 0b11 = 2; 1u << 6 = 64
F16: 4 != 0 is 1, so x & (4 != 0) tests bit 0: for x = 00000100 it gives 0, for 00000001 it gives 1; (x & 4) != 0 for 00000100 gives 1
F18: XOR rows 00 01 10 11 -> 0 1 1 0
F19: row 1,1: OR 1, XOR 0
F20: A AND NOT (B OR C), rows ABC: 000->0 001->0 010->0 011->0 100->1 101->0 110->0 111->0; rows lit: 1 of 8
F21: rows AB: 00:11,00 01:11,00 10:00,11 11:11,11; NOT(A AND NOT B) vs NOT A OR B failures 0; (A AND B) OR (A AND NOT B) vs A failures 0
F22: NOT(A OR B) vs NOT A OR NOT B, rows AB: 00:11 01:01 10:01 11:00; fails in 2 rows
F25: start 14 (even: 1); +4 keeps parity: 1; -10 keeps parity: 1; 21 is even: 0
F26: second printed line with placeValue * 3: rest=22 placeValue=3 doneSoFar=1, rest * placeValue + doneSoFar = 67, holds: 0
F27 (forensic): bytes 04 00 FD F6 EC E2 unsigned: 4 0 253 246 236 226; signed: 4 0 -3 -10 -20 -30; wrong ones minus 256: -3 -10 -20 -30
== Practical ==
P: GSTAT 0x5A = 01011010: ALARM 0, ZONE 5, PUMP 1, LID 0, LEVEL 2; wide mask (status >> 4) & 0b1111 gives 5
P: GSTAT 0xE3 = 11100011: ALARM 1, ZONE 6, PUMP 0, LID 0, LEVEL 3; wide mask (status >> 4) & 0b1111 gives 14
P: GSTAT 0x0D = 00001101: ALARM 0, ZONE 0, PUMP 1, LID 1, LEVEL 1; wide mask (status >> 4) & 0b1111 gives 0
P: GSTAT 0xAB = 10101011: ALARM 1, ZONE 2, PUMP 1, LID 0, LEVEL 3; wide mask (status >> 4) & 0b1111 gives 10
P: TEMP 0xF6 = 11110110 unsigned 246, signed -10
P: TEMP 0x12 = 00010010 unsigned 18, signed 18
P: TEMP 0xEC = 11101100 unsigned 236, signed -20
P: TEMP 0x00 = 00000000 unsigned 0, signed 0
P: encode ALARM 1, ZONE 2, PUMP 1, LID 0, LEVEL 3 -> 10101011 = 0xAB = 171
P: masks: set PUMP on 0xE3 -> 0xEB; clear ALARM on 0xE3 -> 0x63; LID test on 0x0D -> 1
P: packets per day at one every 2 s: 43200; bytes 86400 = 84.375 KiB = 86.4 kB
== Project reference ==
patterns of one byte: 256; 0xFF = 255; 2^16 round trips: 65536
